    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_29",
      "quote": "This systematic review aims to determine the role of age in AT efficacy, identify the optimal age for AT treatment and examine whether the reported outcomes differ between age groups in children with Polysomnography (PSG)-confirmed uncomplicated OSA.",
      "reason": "The aims state the knowledge gap the review will address (role of age, optimal age, differences between age groups), which implies uncertainties in current knowledge, but there is no explicit description of the existing state of knowledge or a detailed discussion of important uncertainties."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_29",
      "quote": "We aimed to provide evidence-based suggestions for precise AT treatment in childhood.",
      "reason": "The text explains the purpose and importance of the review—to provide evidence-based suggestions for precise AT treatment—justifying the need to conduct the review."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No evidence was found describing prior similar systematic reviews, citing them, or explaining the need for the current review as an update or replication."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No text in the provided evidence describes the proposed mechanism of action of adenotonsillectomy."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No logic model or consideration of a logic model showing hypothesised relationships between intervention components and outcomes is present in the retrieved evidence."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "75"
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_4",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_29",
      "quote": "Aim of the systemic review This systematic review aims to determine the role of age in AT efficacy, identify the optimal age for AT treatment and examine whether the reported outcomes differ between age groups in children with Polysomnography (PSG)-confirmed uncomplicated OSA. We aimed to provide evidence-based suggestions for precise AT treatment in childhood. Specific objectives of the systemic review To determine the role of age in AT efficacy. To identify the optimal age for AT treatment. To examine whether the reported outcomes differ between age groups in children with Polysomnography (PSG)-confirmed uncomplicated OSA. To provide evidence-based suggestions for precise AT treatment in childhood.",
      "reason": "The manuscript explicitly states the review aim and lists specific objectives regarding the role of age, optimal age for AT, differences between age groups, and providing evidence-based suggestions."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e2",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No explicit statement of planned comparisons using PICO (or variant) for the intervention is provided in the retrieved evidence; objectives describe aims by age but do not present PICO elements or planned comparison groups."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 90
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_5",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "Studies were included if they met the following criteria: pediatric patients (<18 years) diagnosed with OSA using PSG based on widely accepted diagnostic guidelines at the time of publication and quantitative data available for outcomes of interest before and after surgery. In addition, the study should be published in English, and the study design should be case-control, cohort, randomized controlled trials (RCTs), or before-after studies.",
      "reason": "The eligibility criteria explicitly specify patient age (<18), diagnostic method (PSG), requirement for quantitative pre/post outcomes, language, and eligible study designs."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "In addition, the study should be published in English, and the study design should be case-control, cohort, randomized controlled trials (RCTs), or before-after studies.",
      "reason": "Language restriction (English) is explicitly stated. However, other report characteristics asked for by the item (e.g., dissemination year limits or publication/report status) are not specified as eligibility limits; although year of publication is extracted (text_8), no explicit eligibility restrictions by year or publication status are reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No information is provided distinguishing exclusion because outcomes were not measured from exclusion because outcome results were not reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_11",
      "quote": "To understand the effect of age on AT outcomes, participants were grouped into multiple age thresholds according to study-reported means of 0-5 vs. >5, 0-6 vs. >6, 0-7 vs. >7, and 0-8 vs. >8 years. For studies that stratified patients by age, the original groups were retained. Meta-regression analysis was performed to assess whether age was a significant predictor of AT efficacy. Subgroup analyses were also conducted based on each predefined age category to explore the age differences in response to treatment.",
      "reason": "The review specifies the groups used in syntheses (multiple age thresholds) and links these groups to subgroup/meta-regression analyses addressing the review objective of age effects."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "Studies were excluded if they focused exclusively on complicated pediatric populations, such as those with comorbidities that could independently affect post-operative outcomes. This included studies solely involving children with obesity (body mass index (BMI) \u2265 95th percentile for age and sex), genetic syndromes affecting airway anatomy, craniofacial abnormalities, and neurological or psychiatric disorders impacting cognition or behavior. However, studies with mixed populations were included in this review.",
      "reason": "A rationale is provided for excluding studies of complicated populations: comorbidities could independently affect post-operative outcomes; specific examples of such populations are listed."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 80
}

